       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours would make the effects last.\n\nPlease check whether this is a typo. These are the usual doses:\n- **Usual starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. Use 2.5 mg for frail patients, or if the patient is small or on other antihypertensives.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nIf you meant 5 mg, or 10 mg, tell me and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 50 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
